Independent final review covers all14 changed files and all14 planned cases against original/live14 and full parent8 before reading checker claims. New private accumulator uses mutex-protected bounded per-category evidence independent of optional shared progress; observations are overlapping, not unique item counts. Actual read/parse, initial-object/shader/graphics/compute/raytracing producers, resolver setup, unsupported/validation and missing dependencies retain distinct reasons. Failed iterations and compile-required skip remain failed; successful compile-required fallback remains successful. Queue completed_count remains processed count including failed processing, with real-thread exact queue tests in both contexts. Normal outcomes propagate by actual normal entry and paired internal terminal pipe+nonzero OS status through Linux and Windows controllers. Controlled failures drain orderly siblings, retain reason mask and avoid death/retry counts; existing13 worker-loss/recovery/unknown-range tests remain. Both platform source paths reviewed; native Windows execution explicitly excluded and unverified. Real shipped CLI/ExternalReplayer and private production-entry/controlled-producer tests are meaningful with clean controls, watchdogs, known FOZ readback and deterministic kernel barriers; Release checks use DiagnosticChecks. Preserved public headers/layout/version and existing progress/resume semantics, intentional false-success CLI exit change and additive internal REPLAY_FAILED grammar are documented; no general binary ABI or mixed-version protocol guarantee. Actual old-header caller is freshly compiled from base-first headers and run with candidate library/executable. No helper changes; separate Python helper suite outside planned scope. No generated/private files in source diff. CHANGELOG.md11 is one short [Observability] sentence with practical drained-queue false-success benefit and full correct14 URL; combined historical entries remain accurate. Repaired verification.md565-573 explicitly binds old zero exit to13 delivery and14 supersedes it with orderly1, preserves current parse/skip and zero death counters and Debug E5/E6 worker-loss distinction. Lines585-593 bind unchanged grammar to13 then explicitly add current14 REPLAY_FAILED while preserving caller/layout/progress semantics. Prior I14-C1-DOCS-SUPERSESSION independently confirmed resolved, not omitted. Readiness generation346 exact candidate/base/plan/input marker re-read; only root14 eligible Closes, parent8 remains open. Prepared compare branch is not represented as already pushed. Prerequisite10 PR42 and13 PR67 actual merges agree with retained independent delivery evidence and are ancestors of exact base. No source bookkeeping commit after accepted candidate. These results claim no real driver compilation, Steam behavior, cache warming/persistence/durability, general ABI or whole observability standard compliance.

